ed REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm simple mastectomy specimen  A REMOVED_DATE x 17 0cm skin ellipse is present with an unremarkable nipple  A suture is present demarcating the lateral aspect of the specimen  A REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm well healed irregular shaped scar is present at the lower lateral quadrant of the skin ellipse   5 o clock   As well  an area of green discoloration is present at the 3 o clock portion of the skin ellipse  No definitive axillary tissue is identified on the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm poorly defined  tan white fibrous area with focal gritty firm sections  This region is located posterior to the scar on the surface of the skin and just posterior to the green stained breast parenchyma  This ill defined area is  0 1cm from the posterior margin in the lateral portion of the specimen  It runs along a broad front  A movable layer of fascia is present over the entire area of the region in question  No discrete mass is identified  The remainder of the breast parenchyma has scattered diffuse ill defined tan white and yellow firm fibrous areas  most of which are located in the superior portion of the specimen  No discrete masses are identified  No intraparenchymal lymph nodes are identified either  Section code  C G  representative sections of ill defined fibrous area and adjacent posterior margin  H I  representative sections of fibrous area adjacent to thick portion of 8 0cm localization wire found in breast within main fibrous area  J   representative sections of most fibrous area within green dyed breast parenchyma  K L  more representative section of main fibrous area  M N  representative sections of fibrous tissue in surrounding breast parenchyma  2 0cm from the posterior margin in the medial portion of the specimen  O   representative sections of fibrous areas of breast parenchyma in the lateral portion of the specim