ite firm tissue  close to the posterior resection margin  but mobile under the fascia surface  cassette I   In the axillary tail  no lymph node is definitely identified  There is an area of white fibrous white firm tissue  extending along the tail over 6 0cm  and measuring about 0 5cm in diameter  Representative sections of the tissue are submitted in cassette A B  SECTION CODE  C E  edges of the largest biopsy  relation to posterior margin F G  medial and lateral edges of the largest cavity  no inked margin in the samples  H  largest biopsy cavity I J K  posterior margin of the smallest cavity  relation to posterior margin  L M  small biopsy cavity  N O P  distance breast parenchyma  N closest to the small biopsy cavity  inferior  O and P both from deep inferior internal quadrant  Resident  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  24 AUG 94 at 11 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HIGH GRADE REMOVED_DATE  1 7 CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  CARCINOMA EXTENDS TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED SURFACE  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Vascular and lymphatic invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  26 AUG 94 at 15 41 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  A roentgenogram accompanies the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm ill defined tan mass with stellate radicals which approach an inked margin in multiple areas  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted in cassette A through L  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
