xis of  the specimen runs from superior to inferior  The anterior margin is inked  blue  the posterior margin is inked black  the lateral margin is inked yellow  and the medial margin is inked green  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm pink tan  firm  ill defined mass  which is 2 0cm from the superior margin   2 4cm from the inferior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  1 6cm from  the medial margin  1 2cm from the anterior margin and 1 5cm from the  posterior margin  Further sectioning reveals a spiral metallic clip  Also  noted 1 1cm to the dominant lesion is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  ill defined  nodule  which is 0 5cm from the medial margin  1 0cm from the posterior  margin  2 0cm from the anterior margin  4 0cm from the lateral margin  2 5cm  from the superior and 2 0cm from the inferior margin  The remainder of the  specimen is composed of gray white  rubbery  focally granular  fibrous tissue  admixed with yellow  soft  lobulated  adipose tissue  Representative sections  are submitted from superior to inferior as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin  en face    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger mass to anterior and lateral margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger mass to posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger mass to medial margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger mass  with accompanying medial margin  with clip site    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller mass to medial and posterior margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening tissue between 2 masses    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin  bisected  en face     Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast lumpectomy  deep margin   are 2 unoriented pieces of tan yellow  focally hemorrhagic   fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE and 3 6cm in maximum dimension  both of  which are inked black and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Receive