EMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm biopsy cavity  located deep to the semi circular cutaneous scar  The biopsy cavity is lined by a rim of white yellow calcified  relatively firm tissue  Along the deep and posterior portion of the biopsy cavity is an area of white  firm tissue  measuring in maximal section REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and extending for an approximate length of 7 0cm along the edge of the biopsy cavity  The closest margin is the deep resection margin within approximately 2 5cm of the biopsy cavity  The firm area is subjacent to the nipple area  Section code  A C  area of firmness adjacent to biopsy cavity D  probable tumor involving nipple E H  closest deep resection margin I  closest superficial resection margin J L N  lymph nodes Labeled  right breast  are two resection specimens  The larger specimen is a 27  0x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm breast mastectomy  oriented with a short stitch designating its superior aspect  that is now inked blue and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  Overlying the mastectomy specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm ellipse of white pink skin  centered by a 4 5cm in maximal diameter areola  The areola is firm with no grossly evident nipple but central dimpling  Located medially on the skin ellipse is a semi circular 4 5cm long  well healed linear scar  A second scar  measuring approximately 3 5cm in length  well healed  is located in the inferolateral margin of the skin ellipse  The deep resection margin of the specimen is inked green  The inferior resection margin is inked black  and the superior resection margin is inked blue  Along the inferior resection margin is an open area that leads into a biopsy cavity  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity communicating through the previously described orifice with the antero inferior surface of the specimen  The biopsy cavity is filled with red fluid  has smooth walls covered by brown  irregular surface and is surrounded by white firm  fibrous tissue that radiates into numerous bands that reach the inked deep and inferior resection margin in multiple points  The firmest portion of the biopsy cavity is superiorly located  deep to the nipple  measures approximately 2 5cm in maximal diameter and extends to the superior resection margin  Section code  M O  biopsy cavity in area open to inferior resection margin P R  biopsy cavity  areas of firmness with relation to nipple in Q  nipple R T  firm breast parenchyma  representative sections T  superior resection margin in relation to firm area U  biopsy cavity in relation to deep resection margin In the same container is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE ellipse of white pink skin  with an eccentric 5 0cm long well healed semi circular scar  touching one of the skin margins  excised to a maximum depth of 1 0cm  The deep resection margin is inked black  the superior resection margin is inked blue  The specimen is not oriented  Sectioning reveals a focal area of fat necrosis  No tumor masses are identified  Representative sections through the area of fat necrosis are submitted in cassettes V Y  Labeled  right axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm adipose tissue containing numerous lymph nodes  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassettes Z through BB  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  Edi Brogi  M D   PhD  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
