ed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 14 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm fibroadipose breast tissue with one stitch indicating the medial deep margin as designated by the surgeon  A needle guide wire is in place and removed  The specimen is inked black on the medial aspect  blue on the lateral aspect  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  white tan mostly ill defined  mass which extends to within 0 2cm to a medial  black  margin  0 7cm away from the area marked by a stitch  The minimal distance to the other margin is REMOVED_DATE  and 1 5cm  The remainder of the specimen consists of lobular fat with thin fibrous strands  Section code  A C  nodule  entirely submitted with margins  D E  breast tissue with fibrous strands adjacent to the lesion F H  further representative sections of breast tissue away from lesion  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  deep margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unoriented fibrous tissue which is inked black  sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes I J  Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kathleen Ann Mccarthy  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  MASS    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   DEEP MARGIN , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 40 CLINICAL DATA  Inflammatory changes on physical exam with skin thickening and upper outer quadrant mass on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  PLEOMORPHIC TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definitive lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The tumor consists of pleomorphic cells growing in cords and clusters with a high mitotic rate and occasional intracytoplasmic lumina  Focally  the tumor resembles a high grade infiltrating ductal type carcinoma  although the predominant features are those of a pleomorphic infiltrating lobular carcinoma  Immunohistochemical stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported separately  Dr  Frederick Koerner has reviewed selected slides and agrees with the interpretation  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 39                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 29     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     Tumor does not extend to the overlying skin  dermis or epidermis   Added by  Anthony Mattia  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm overlying ellipse of skin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular firm white lesion  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in maximum dimension  2 0cm deep to the skin ellipse  A representative section of the lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted in A through K  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
