htly cystic  well circumscribed mass  In this area a metal clip is identified  Mass  2 is 1 1cm from the posterior margin and 3 0cm from the anterior margin  Mass  3 is a 0 6cm from mass  2  and focally adjacent to mass  1  Mass  3 is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan well circumscribed mass that is 1 5cm from the anterior margin and 1 5cm from the posterior margin  There is a metal clip identified in mass  3  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow  lobulated to focally fibrotic and unremarkable  The upper outer quadrant breast tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are gross identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  1 to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  1 to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  1 to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of mass  1 in relationship to mass  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  2 to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section of mass  2 to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  2 in relationship to mass  3 and posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  3 to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  3 to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma to posterior margin  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  1A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SENTINEL  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE  LEFT NON SENTINEL  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The 