en receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate parts  Labeled  Right breast   1  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with needle localizing wire in place  and accompanying specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan  firm mass with ill defined borders  that extends to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in A through F  with the tumor mass in A through C  Labeled  Right breast  2  is a 3 x 2 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with needle localizing wire in place and accompanying specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a pink tan  firm  speckled white mass  that extends to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  2  and saved frozen  The remaining specimen is submitted entirely in G through J  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT BREAST  2  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Craig Scott Seidman  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
