eper sections for receptor protein immunohistochemical analysis due to the small size  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm excisional breast specimen  The surgeon denotes the superior margin with a short stitch  and the lateral margin with a long stitch  The long axis of the specimen is in the medial to lateral direction  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior blue  superior   green  inferior   yellow  Within the specimen there is a localization wire with a report that calcifications are along the proximal part of the thick wire  This area is in the more medial part of the specimen  In the lateral area of the specimen there appears to be a separate area of calcifications based on the specimen radiograph  The parenchyma is yellowish pink and unremarkable without nodules or masses  The following cassettes are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral en face resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial en face resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections near area of calcification of thick segment of wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections in the more lateral area with possible calcifications  Gross Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Christine Garcia M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The deeper sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not contain invasive lobular carcinoma tumor cells  The lobular carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen and proges