Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1   REMOVED_DATE CM  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  SCANT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm tan yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a O 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white  firm  stellate area adjacent to the resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable and is composed of predominantly of adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through J  with the stellate area in cassettes A through E  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 42 CLINICAL DATA  A 58 year old woman with suspicious calcifications within the left breast and a biopsy showed carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY    RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ABOUT BIOPSY SITE  SOLID  CRIBRIFORM  AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES   SEE NOTE     FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA    FIBROADENOMA  0 5 CM     FAT NECROSIS  FIBROSIS  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE    SKIN WITH SCAR    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWENTY FIVE OF TWENTY FIVE LYMPH NODES  0 25   NOTE  The resection margins are free of tumor  No invasive component is seen  LYMPH NODE  BIOPSY    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 31                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  left modified mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 8cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an axillary tail  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm  There is a curved healed skin incision line  measuring 5 0cm in the superior medial quadrant  The overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 11 5cm and the nipple is everted and measures 4 0cm from the inferior margin and 11 0cm from the lateral margin  The previously described incision line is 2 0cm from the superior margin and 1 2cm from the medial skin margin  The skin is grossly unremarkable  On sectioning through the breast  there is a large REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm blood filled cavity  Its wall is red brown with adherent green tan and fibrinous exudates  The tissue at the periphery of the wall is firm but sharply delineated  No grossly evident invasive lesion is identified  This cavity is 3 5cm from the closest deep margin  3 0cm from the closest inferior margin  4 0cm from the closest superior margin  and 3 5cm deep to the skin ellipse  Sectioning through the remainder of the breast parenchyma reveals unremarkable fatty breast tissue with scattered areas of white  rubbery  fibrous tissue with intermixed pink tan speckles representing breast lobules  No other localized lesions are identified in the remaining breast tissue  Section Code A   Representative sections of deep margin  B G   Representative sections from around the biopsy cavity  H   Representative sections from the medial half of the breast  I   Representative sections from the central portion of the breast  J   Representative sections from the lateral portion of the breast  K   Skin incision and superior margin  L M   Nipple  N BB DD   Axillary lymph nodes  the largest of which measures 4 0cm in greatest diameter  Most of these nodes are very fatty and fleshy  Note  Cassettes U and W BB and DD each represent one lymph node each  Also received in the same specimen container is a specimen jar  labeled  lymph node   It contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of adipose tissue and intermixed lymph node  It is submitted entirely in cassette CC  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley Souba  MD Noah Chan H Choi  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST AND LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES , Unchecked.
