d by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mass of fibroadipose tissue which has been oriented by the surgeon  a short stitch marks the superior end  and the long stitch the lateral margins  The specimen is inked as follows  Black medial  blue lateral  orange superior  Multiple cut sections show a firm white tumor mass with a maximum diameter of 2 5cm which closely approaches the superior medial and inferior medial margins  Representative sections are submitted going from the medial to the lateral portion of the specimen as follows  Section codes  A  most medial B C  adjacent to most medial D F  superior G H  inferior I J  lateral  A J are taken from the superficial portion of the specimen K O  sections from deep portion of specimen going from medial to lateral  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white tan portion of adipose and lymphoid tissue  bisected and entirely submitted in P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary nonsentinel node  are two pieces of yellow tan fibroadipose and lymphoid tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm   The specimens are bisected and entirely submitted in Q  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  additional superomedial margin  