agnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margins  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm cystic space containing a gray to tan yellow friable material  The cyst wall is gray pink  fibrous  and averages less than 0 1cm in thickness  The cystic structure focally abuts the postero inferior margin and comes to 1 0cm of the anterior  4 0cm of the superior  and more than 2cm of the medial and lateral margins  Abutting the cyst along the posterosuperior aspect  is a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm indurated gray white lobulated mass which comes to 0 5cm of the posterior  1 2cm of the inferior  1 3cm of the anterior  3 7cm of the superior  and 1 7cm of the lateral  and greater than 2cm of the medial margin  Along the anterosuperior aspect of the indurated lesion is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic space containing a soft tan brown substance  The space is consistent with previous biopsy site and is surrounded by focal bright yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  The space comes to 0 3cm of the anterior  REMOVED_DATE of the superior  2 0cm of the inferior  1 4cm of the posterior  1 7cm of the lateral  and greater than 2cm of the medial margins  One of the localization wires is located in the tissue immediately medial to the indurated lesion and cavity  The second localization wire is located 1 2cm medial to the first wire  The cross sections are taken to breast imaging and radiographed  The remaining dense gray white fibrous tissue shows focal gritty areas  Representative section is submitted  from