Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  14 AUG 98 at 15 03 CLINICAL DATA  None                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CELL BLOCK  ADENOCARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  A mucicarmine stain was performed and shows cytoplasmic mucin vacuoles in some cells  There is no background mucin or mucin in a stromal fragment  The morphology of the cells is most consistent with lobular carcinoma  but ductal carcinoma cannot be completely excluded  See also cytology specimen number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Diagnosis by  Barbara Centeno  M D  Signed On  19 AUG 98 at 18 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm soft  tan pink gelatinous pellet which is submitted in toto as Cassette A  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  CYTOPATHOLOGY STAFF  A B                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Leonard Lloyd Ellman  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CELLBLOCK   report_end  , Unchecked.
