100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm modified mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm skin ellipse with a retracted nipple and stitch marking 12 o clock position  The resection margins are inked black and the lateral anterior half is double inked blue  and the medial anterior half is double inked green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm irregularly shaped white stellate hard mass with fibrous strands the extend to the deep inferior margins and extend to within 0 5cm of the posterior deep resection margin  Four representative sections from mass  from lateral to medial  approximately 1 0cm apart are submitted in cassettes A through D  respectively  A section of the posterior inferior margin at the lateral half are submitted in cassette E  A section of the tumor near the posterior margin is submitted in cassette F  A section of the medial inferior posterior margin is submitted in cassette G  A dissection of the axillary tail yeilded lymph nodes of varying sizes ranging from REMOVED_DATE up to 1 8cm  submitted in cassettes H through J  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
